{"posts":[{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1051","t":"Second chart\n\nAnd 1 chart: 2 compressions:)","a":"greywind5","d":"","n":"#1051","p":43,"im":["3ab76b05892072f943332520f0b46a565ee2b3ad","742fdeff92776ca17d87971ce0c89100cbe1d865"],"m":1051},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1052","t":"Another one, with Liquidity, and an \"anomaly\" in how price goes through the CP.","a":"greywind5","d":"","n":"#1052","p":43,"im":["3870b4344786055693481ae81f5420472f71adb0"],"m":1052},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1053","t":"Some other charts with CP. I notice that I have quite a hard time spotting these CP. I know they are \"everywhere\", but my mind makes me look only for the best looking ones, which limits my findings to only the winner setups. I feel like I'm not learning them the way I should.","a":"greywind5","d":"","n":"#1053","p":43,"im":["82ffc58a2cbfdc5010cf4b17bd03abd6df4db1e3","7e5665ea36d8e7a11fdf9f3696e0531d66816417","6fac219c6a627410165a2f1bc02e62facabc19ff"],"m":1053},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1054","t":"Hello!\n\nI have began my homework on compression. This are my first 10 compressions. I would be glad to see some opinions, critiques, feedback from you.","a":"Trader05","d":"","n":"#1054","p":43,"im":["6546f44a1644c2ad7a800c1863e6822c28a8d7ca","4121de008803f5cce89c7258341265d123614426","dc2c0123f0f5d2bd2eeb578d322b63826ae97140","f2c882520005dfed203fa764ae3a07ffc58ab29a","047f0c57917bdc811bdaf46442b5a401b765680e","3841f691211cb713e5805fa12cdf95e9ba4e2e53"],"m":1054},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1055","t":"A beautiful one in my opinion.","a":"greywind5","d":"","n":"#1055","p":43,"im":["c5e8c8b2c9898b57261c09425dba98e0e3302ffd"],"m":1055},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1056","t":"Yep, really nice.","a":"Trader05","d":"","n":"#1056","p":43,"im":[],"m":1056},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1057","t":"Another 10\n\nI dont't know what to say about this. It looks simple from the left side of the chart but I think I need a little more practice until I will be able to recognize it in real time.","a":"Trader05","d":"","n":"#1057","p":43,"im":["b7c3bbf87f67cad6c784e987c41c996ee2a45fc0","2aaea62d4fb42d96fe0481c86c840e808bb74b44","5e41acba6d70135f7d63cf3d1ab5ab1e5d96fc45","607540620a6487f52bac0d52e6c24f66f4806673","15ebe8b0df9f3927e252dc9487b1e45b582145f7","c99735ba168bea38b2f757bb167818a95da873c8","3b725ab898532a64fd7474c463295ca8cdb4b198","9821b5c26b74d1ccbe4355f25fe541588504a062","1e5a6dd6be318505539f7dcdb9fd3bb7d868931e"],"m":1057},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1058","t":"Another more\n\nI really need one of the masters opinion here....","a":"Trader05","d":"","n":"#1058","p":43,"im":["c062c1c9c648c005fa4176b274be86f903a04987","20fd62bced24a11720a9acb239e7754546e169e1","d0de6be60f3724bbc065c7cd7bc92178945a48ce","672652b244f2af2271ab1ba3e24308c1c19a94e7","4c1ac5a276bee7e7e306aa6a199b6a57e3019bd7","7c0b4639b4baf6c367fff2eb43e57a5eedd9ea2a","689cd8f4d8f3302de094ff5a5b68f0089c3958d8"],"m":1058},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1059","t":"This is my last post about compression (for now). From now, I'll read what others have been doing about it. I felt important not to look at the work of others before trying to find CPs myself.","a":"greywind5","d":"","n":"#1059","p":43,"im":["6664cf995ff489f55ec9d9e6118a065e492d6c5f","86021bfa3af95302b3e05a43ecdcd359cb764d4d","baa5ce1c5fb2e26f68163ff703dda858cea6ce3b"],"m":1059},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1060","t":"Ok. I read the thread and it seems easier to spot them now.\n\nI finished this homework, and the last chart is a nice transition to the next homework: QM!:)","a":"greywind5","d":"","n":"#1060","p":43,"im":["eadb2307728d8a504efc3960046491194adf8fc2","e4619431495de225cf6a1267ca78c0ffe1ea0309"],"m":1060},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1061","t":"Posting up some homework i enjoyed this one.. One question I have if someone knows the answer! Sometimes when compression ends it takes off in the same direction that the compression was moving vs coming back through it. Is there a way to see this coming??","a":"Duds","d":"","n":"#1061","p":43,"im":["75134eebe1b156b6db679d5f31696bb2c1b41731","26b6f8112679074ca53f8b4606cc2dc43c909a41","8b7f6b11118046745ce0c7e066bb8514f2c9a804","252911ed27117dc2230a984d26945a0439fb6b84","c729534d681d3267659f0ea967cbc136c0be372c","9b24a09719a751efd351dee12ec49ab465335b8c","7a25c15d7fb71c7ca40b3e821b470a3ce6182765","9aa846ae2e855e2dd588fda3a1ee062a092329a4"],"m":1061},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1062","t":"Hey friend I'm glad to see you post your homework, it seems you're even going faster than me, and you're doing a great job\n\nTo answer your question, I think Compression doesn't tell us the way market is going to go once it touches the next FTR, It can simply ignore that FTR and go to the next. What we know for sure, is that all buy orders (in bull CP example) have been cleared so when price breaks back into that compression, it will be very likely to see price going through in short amount of time.\n\nAlert: newbie answer.","a":"greywind5","d":"","n":"#1062","p":43,"im":[],"m":1062},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1063","t":"we're thinking about how we don't know how to use them. Tell us about one of simple, is it?","a":"TRADER48","d":"","n":"#1063","p":43,"im":["abe22e7694b765f9ea127e666a958b1c399e549e"],"m":1063},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1064","t":"Afternoon all,\n\nI've not had much time to post since my last visit but I have been doing homework when I can.\n\nI've been taking it slow initially, knowing myself, I have a tendancy to jump straight in with a little knowledge. I'm trying to make sure I understand the concept and the reasoning behind it rather than 'that's what happens when the price reaches there'.\n\nWhat I have found so far is that courage in your conviction is essential.\n\nI will hopefully be able to post more of my homework from this week forwards, as well as live trades (small amounts) to help me learn not only the markets but myself and how I react.\n\nA question about the chart I have posted, as you can see it's just the 5min chart, when you have a min stop distance and it is beyond where you would like your stop, from your experience what would you do? Not trade such low timeframes, place a stop and move it as and when the price moves in a favorable driection or just watch and stop yourself out when the trades moves to your stop point as you're probably going to be watching on such a low timeframe trade anyway?\n\nMay not be the right place for the above question but I applied it to the chart I have a attached.\n\nCheers,\n\nRobbie","a":"Rdk123","d":"","n":"#1064","p":43,"im":[],"m":1064},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1065","t":"","a":"Rdk123","d":"","n":"#1065","p":43,"im":["e46cd153715585e37a2d54f02758c1efa93bc6de"],"m":1065},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1066","t":"Practice","a":"Experiorz","d":"","n":"#1066","p":43,"im":["19f2b72cc901b83e72922b2464b34667c69ab697","ce5dabc093c68343a3eb25355cb91559d754fe9c"],"fa":"تمرین","m":1066},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1067","t":"Practice","a":"Experiorz","d":"","n":"#1067","p":43,"im":["5b592fc61999276bc2fb1284537c380445b7b376","01b11664cc7601b696e8c34b91c9837795815a82","f5da801794487406db0e67d90e6279723b976252"],"fa":"تمرین","m":1067},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1068","t":"Practice","a":"Experiorz","d":"","n":"#1068","p":43,"im":["5b592fc61999276bc2fb1284537c380445b7b376","01b11664cc7601b696e8c34b91c9837795815a82","f5da801794487406db0e67d90e6279723b976252"],"fa":"تمرین","m":1068},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1069","t":"Hi\n\nHere's my first set of compression homework. Feel free to comment good or bad. Time has been a premium for me lately though I have spent many hours trawling the journals. I thought I should do some more homework so more of it makes sense.\n\nThanks","a":"fxsniper","d":"","n":"#1069","p":43,"im":["2892d6ffa566449f243013085ebfa0aa990ea368","bcd4e0573c756431eefd1292bd028782ddaee0a4","627d2020099c295a01534e60d264998a8271786b","ee1645540b2ae2004b25807a8bf0b9467863bb4b","133e7190f90afaeeccd33361afef40b29c67f9f5","f1c8b5c889edb733ef2b12ed22288a1b322b2131","0781ba2536159f5bfae33c01a2721ce35431390f"],"m":1069},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1070","t":"I clicked on the \"here\" link but it brought me to the acegazzette website and say \"error 404\".\n\nHow can i see what is being shown?\n\nThank you\n\nwhiteout wrote:\n\nActs 28 wrote: First of all thanks for the analysis, can I ask you when you write This= Taken out, do you mean taking out the previous Supply/Demand level? Thank in advance!!","a":"Bodostock","d":"","n":"#1070","p":43,"im":[],"m":1070},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1071","t":"As much as I know Acegazette is completely transformed for something else. don't know if this link should work any more.","a":"benhur","d":"","n":"#1071","p":43,"im":[],"m":1071},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1072","t":"Ifmyante wrote: Yes, once price got below the highest clean demand, it was free to run through the CP zone to the next clean Demand\n\nMy english ain't that good.\n\nDon't really understand this statement.\n\n\"price got below the highest clean demand\" - Thought that demand is always at the bottom, what does it mean by highest?\n\nCan someone post a chart to show the meaning of the above statement?\n\nThank you.\n\nRegards","a":"Bodostock","d":"","n":"#1072","p":43,"im":[],"m":1072},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1073","t":"Hey there Bod,\n\nI do believe IF was answering this post here readthemarket.com/index.php/forum/homewo...sion?limitstart=0#45\n\nThe image in the post, reveals this","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#1073","p":43,"im":["6e60c65931c43acfdafde1bad7386b5bda91e68c"],"m":1073},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1074","t":"Hi naascott,\n\nThanks for posting the chart.\n\nThat area highlighted by you - isn't it a RBD decision point / supply zone?\n\nI have read in couple of postings where members mentioned about clean demand and supply or fresh demand and supply.\n\nHow do we read the chart to know what is clean and fresh?\n\nIs there any thread that talk about this topic?\n\nFor example how is it that the area you highlighted is considered \"clean\"?\n\nThank you\n\nnaascott wrote: Hey there Bod,\n\nI do believe IF was answering this post here readthemarket.com/index.php/forum/homewo...sion?limitstart=0#45\n\nThe image in the post, reveals this","a":"Bodostock","d":"","n":"#1074","p":43,"im":["6e60c65931c43acfdafde1bad7386b5bda91e68c"],"m":1074},{"id":"aboutcompression_p43_1075","t":"Hello Bodostock,\n\nI didn't highlight those areas. Apparently, the fella who posted the image had done so. Taking a close look on a lower time frame in this area, it appears (at least to me) that the highest clean demand was actually above that area. I am still learning as you, and I just posted what seemed to be obvious. Always good to get another opinion, too.:)\n\nP.S. MT4 may not let you view history this far back below the m15. For this reason, I used Forex tester","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#1075","p":43,"im":["4f3fc9b7d53a48d5cb6747ebfa93ccb12087eee2"],"m":1075}],"images":[{"k":"3ab76b05892072f943332520f0b46a565ee2b3ad","t":"assets/thumbs/3ab76b05892072f943332520f0b46a565ee2b3ad.webp","f":"assets/images/3ab76b05892072f943332520f0b46a565ee2b3ad.jpeg","w":1500,"h":673,"b":45893,"o":"3ab76b05892072f943332520f0b46a565ee2b3ad.jpeg","p":43,"pid":"aboutcompression_p43_1051"},{"k":"742fdeff92776ca17d87971ce0c89100cbe1d865","t":"assets/thumbs/742fdeff92776ca17d87971ce0c89100cbe1d865.webp","f":"assets/images/742fdeff92776ca17d87971ce0c89100cbe1d865.jpeg","w":1500,"h":668,"b":51286,"o":"742fdeff92776ca17d87971ce0c89100cbe1d865.jpeg","p":43,"pid":"aboutcompression_p43_1051"},{"k":"3870b4344786055693481ae81f5420472f71adb0","t":"assets/thumbs/3870b4344786055693481ae81f5420472f71adb0.webp","f":"assets/images/3870b4344786055693481ae81f5420472f71adb0.jpeg","w":1500,"h":667,"b":53580,"o":"3870b4344786055693481ae81f5420472f71adb0.jpeg","p":43,"pid":"aboutcompression_p43_1052"},{"k":"82ffc58a2cbfdc5010cf4b17bd03abd6df4db1e3","t":"assets/thumbs/82ffc58a2cbfdc5010cf4b17bd03abd6df4db1e3.webp","f":"assets/ima